WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:06.360
Where in the brain does a function live?

2
00:00:07.380 --> 00:00:08.380
Start with the map.

3
00:00:08.960 --> 00:00:15.040
From the side, the cerebral cortex divides into four lobes: frontal, parietal,

4
00:00:15.720 --> 00:00:17.220
temporal and occipital.

5
00:00:18.240 --> 00:00:21.000
The brainstem and the cerebellum sit beside them.

6
00:00:21.820 --> 00:00:23.460
A map names places.

7
00:00:24.060 --> 00:00:26.400
It does not tell you what lives in each one.

8
00:00:27.200 --> 00:00:29.140
Read the map literally.

9
00:00:29.880 --> 00:00:33.520
The precentral gyrus contains primary motor cortex.

10
00:00:34.240 --> 00:00:38.440
The postcentral gyrus contains primary somatosensory cortex.

11
00:00:39.340 --> 00:00:44.640
No region here has a single function, and no function lives in a single region.

12
00:00:45.360 --> 00:00:46.900
The cortex is a mosaic.

13
00:00:47.940 --> 00:00:54.400
One atlas of healthy young adults divides each hemisphere into 180 areas, and

14
00:00:54.400 --> 00:00:56.040
borders vary between people.

15
00:00:56.883 --> 00:01:00.223
So what kind of experiment can place a function?

16
00:01:01.023 --> 00:01:02.523
The first is a lesion.

17
00:01:03.083 --> 00:01:06.463
You compare behaviour before and after damage.

18
00:01:07.083 --> 00:01:11.003
A deficit shows the damaged tissue contributes to the task.

19
00:01:11.823 --> 00:01:13.123
But damage spreads.

20
00:01:14.023 --> 00:01:19.923
In a 1957 report on human patients, several medial temporal structures were removed

21
00:01:19.923 --> 00:01:23.963
at once. The memory loss could not be pinned to one.

22
00:01:24.817 --> 00:01:26.897
The second kind is a recording.

23
00:01:27.877 --> 00:01:30.417
Firing goes with a stimulus or a choice.

24
00:01:30.957 --> 00:01:33.177
That does not show the brain uses it.

25
00:01:34.037 --> 00:01:35.597
The third kind is imaging.

26
00:01:36.357 --> 00:01:39.897
A BOLD fMRI signal measures blood oxygenation.

27
00:01:40.637 --> 00:01:45.917
In anaesthetized macaque visual cortex, it followed local field potentials better

28
00:01:45.917 --> 00:01:51.137
than spiking. An activation does not mark a region as the seat of anything.

29
00:01:52.050 --> 00:01:54.530
The fourth kind adds activity.

30
00:01:55.490 --> 00:01:59.170
Rhesus monkeys judged the direction of noisy moving dots.

31
00:02:00.290 --> 00:02:05.870
Salzman, Newsome and their colleagues stimulated neurons in area MT that shared a

32
00:02:05.870 --> 00:02:06.910
preferred direction.

33
00:02:07.770 --> 00:02:13.170
In 139 experiments, stimulation had a significant effect in 89.

34
00:02:13.890 --> 00:02:17.910
In 86 of those, choices moved toward the preferred direction.

35
00:02:17.910 --> 00:02:25.310
That shows a contribution, in that task, from the stimulated neurons, not from one cell type.

37
00:02:25.600 --> 00:02:31.780
Here is the rule. A lesion shows contribution, not which part of the damage

38
00:02:31.780 --> 00:02:36.600
mattered. A recording shows covariation, not use.

39
00:02:38.120 --> 00:02:42.420
Imaging shows where a blood signal goes, not which neural signal.

40
00:02:43.600 --> 00:02:47.920
Stimulation shows contribution, not that the region is required.

41
00:02:49.020 --> 00:02:51.200
Claim only what the evidence licenses.
